  "short_task": "# PostgreSQL JOB 5 knobs\n\nTask ID: `knob_http_surrogate_pg_5`.\n\nTune 5 PostgreSQL settings for a JOB analytical join-query workload to minimize predicted query latency. A fixed, previously built surrogate predicts performance; optimization does not execute a live database workload.\n\nObjective: minimize `latency`.\n\nBudget: 50 shared initial observations and 200 new evaluations (250 total).\n\n## Submission\n\n1. Submit all 5 settings as floating-point numbers u in [0,1]. Names identify real database settings, but physical values and enumeration labels from the table must not be submitted directly.\n2. For integer settings, decode as round(min + u*(max-min)). For physical floating-point settings, decode as min + u*(max-min) without rounding.\n3. For K enumeration options, divide [0,1] into K equal-width intervals. Select enum_values[min(floor(u*K),K-1)] using zero-based indexing; u=1 selects the last option. Option order does not imply a performance ranking.\n4. Encoding example: backend_flush_after has physical range 0...256; input 0.25 decodes to 64. This illustrates encoding, not a recommended configuration.\n\n## Parameters\n\nEvery submitted parameter is a float in [0,1]. Physical definitions below are decoded using the rules above; they are not direct submission values.\n\n| Parameter | Meaning | Physical definition | Default |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `backend_flush_after` | Amount written by one backend before requesting operating-system writeback. | Integer: `0` to `256` | `0` |\n| `checkpoint_completion_target` | Fraction of the checkpoint interval over which checkpoint writes are spread. | Float: `0.0` to `1.0` | `0.5` |\n| `max_worker_processes` | Maximum background worker processes supported by the server. | Integer: `0` to `262143` | `8` |\n| `shared_buffers` | Memory allocated to shared database-page buffers. | Integer: `16` to `1000000` | `1024` |\n| `wal_buffers` | Shared buffer space for WAL data; physical value -1 selects automatic sizing. | Integer: `-1` to `262143` | `-1` |\n\n## Read details as needed\n\nThere are 5 active parameters. get_search_space supports names, query, optional annotated groups and paged index/details views.\n\nget_task_context sections: overview, submission, scoring, mechanisms, domain_knowledge, additional. Read scoring rules and relevant mechanisms before choosing a candidate.\n\nget_trial_history and get_incumbent return scores first; request parameter_names to inspect selected values.\n\nFollow instructions.md: submit_candidate accepts a full config or workspace JSON file directly; write_candidate is optional.\n",
